Target host pidfd compatibility check (2026-09-12)

Host: marslab-server
Kernel: 6.8.0-137-generic

Cross-compiled Linux test binaries executed on target:
- cmd/vela-validation-runtime-launcher: TestRecvFrameStopsWhenContextIsCanceled PASS; TestRecvFrameReturnsEOFOnPeerClose PASS.
- internal/runtimechannel: TestPollLivePIDFDActualProcessExit PASS; TestPollLivePIDFDProcessHelper PASS; TestSameLiveProcessReportsPidfdFilesystem PASS; TestSameLiveProcessRejectsDifferentLegacyPIDFD PASS.

The target exposes modern pidfs for pidfd_open. The implementation retains the compatibility branch for older anon_inode:[pidfd] kernels: it validates /proc/self/fdinfo Pid/NSpid and compares that identity, without reacquiring numeric PIDs. A kernel without pidfd_open and without a valid legacy pidfd identity remains fail-closed; this host run cannot emulate that missing-kernel case.
